  # Level 4 Income Checkpoints

  ## Summary

  Add a 160×160 Level 4 based on Level 3’s armies, wallets, victory condition, and full roster. Level 4
  introduces exactly three capturable checkpoints—dwarven mountain, elven forest, and orc plains—while
  Levels 1–3 retain their current behavior.

  Player base income is 10 gold/second and enemy base income is 15 gold/second. Each checkpoint adds 5
  gold/second to its green or red owner, allowing totals of 25 and 30 respectively.

  ## Core Implementation

  - Extend LevelConfig with player/enemy income rates and checkpoint enablement. Existing levels use
    20/20 income with checkpoints disabled.

  - Add a Checkpoint model containing position, native faction/terrain, current owner, capture
    progress, spawn timer, and associated defender IDs.

  - Generate one checkpoint in each non-path biome:
      - Keep its footprint entirely on its native terrain and outside protected base zones.
      - Select deterministic positions from the terrain seed, separated from bases and one another.
      - Generate a road spur from the existing network to an adjacent cell, never converting the
        checkpoint footprint itself into path terrain.

  - Start each checkpoint native-owned with three melee and two ranged defenders. While native-owned,
    spawn one alternating melee/ranged defender every 30 seconds up to 15 living associated units. Stop
    spawning permanently once green or red captures it.

  - Native defenders remain within a 12-tile checkpoint leash, attack nearby green/red forces, and
    return to their posts when threats leave.

