  - Generalize hostility, targeting, visibility, combat effects, and rendering so native defenders can
    fight both green and red without becoming recruitable or commandable.

  - Generalize AI objectives from only the Verdant King to checkpoints or the king.
  - On Level 4, red prioritizes green-owned checkpoints, then native checkpoints, and attacks the king
    only when all three checkpoints are red-owned. A surviving wave proceeds to the next checkpoint
    after capturing its target.

  - Checkpoint waves bypass the existing 6,000-gold launch requirement. Launch only when estimated wave
    strength is at least 1.35× the target’s living defenders, using the extended combat-strength model.

  - Reduce the Level 4 rally ceiling to eight seconds once strength-qualified and tune the starting
    target selection so the inherited red army plus its first affordable recruit launches within 30
    simulated seconds. Preserve the existing Level 3 AI thresholds and behavior.

  - Red receives checkpoint income under the same rules as green.

  ## UI and Validation

  - Add Level 4 metadata, story copy, difficulty, and preview to the selector; convert the selector to
    a responsive 2×2 card layout at 1280×720.

  - Add tests covering:
      - Level 4 configuration and unchanged Levels 1–3 behavior.
      - Deterministic one-per-biome placement, checkpoint/path separation, adjacent road access, and
        retry seed stability.

      - Initial 3/2 defender composition, 30-second spawning, 15-unit cap, casualty replacement,
        leashing, and spawning stopping after capture.

      - Five-second capture, contested/reset behavior, recapture, and 10/15 base plus 5-per-checkpoint
        income.

      - Native targeting, fog visibility, unique stats, and combat.
      - Level 4 AI checkpoint priority, sub-6,000 early launch, 1.35 strength gate, capture
        transitions, and eventual king targeting.

  - Run the full unit suite and integrated performance benchmark on the 160×160 map.
  - Capture level-select and in-game checkpoint screenshots only under /work/screenshots; inspect every
